                    <msPart xml:id="p2">
                        <msIdentifier/>
                        <msContents><summary>Prayers, Maṣḥafa Taklil, Maṣḥafa Qandil, Catholic Prayers for the Deceased and Litanies</summary>
                            <msItem xml:id="p2_i1">
                                <locus from="49r" to="59r"/>
                                <title type="incomplete" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT5646Mastagabe">Mastagābǝʾ</title>
                                <note>The text starts and ends abruptly. The places, which are reserved for the rubrications have been left empty. It is a 
                                    multiple-type collection of Dǝggʷā-type antiphons, even though Stefan Strelcyn described this set of texts as ‘prières’ 
                                    (= ‘prayers’) in <bibl corresp="http://zotero.org/groups/358366/items/N6HPGQK3"><seg type="book"><!-- attributes from original bibl--></seg><ptr target="bm:Strelcyn1976Catalogue"/><title level="m">Catalogue des manuscrits éthiopiens de l’Accademia Nazionale dei Lincei: Fonds Conti Rossini et Fonds Caetani 209, 375, 376, 377, 378</title><title level="s">Indici e Sussidi Bibliografici della Biblioteca</title><author><forename>Stefan</forename><surname>Strelcyn</surname></author><pubPlace>Roma</pubPlace><publisher>Accademia Nazionale dei Lincei</publisher><date>1976</date><series><title level="s">Indici e Sussidi Bibliografici della Biblioteca</title><biblScope unit="volume">9</biblScope></series><biblScope unit="volume">9</biblScope><note type="tags"><note type="tag">Cataloguing</note><note type="tag">Ethiopic</note><note type="tag">bm:IHABook182</note><note type="tag">bm:Strelcyn1976Catalogue</note></note><note type="tag">Cataloguing</note><note type="tag">Ethiopic</note><note type="tag">bm:IHABook182</note><note type="tag">bm:Strelcyn1976Catalogue</note><citedRange unit="item">77</citedRange><citedRange unit="page">201</citedRange></bibl>. The texts have been arranged according to the days of the week
                                    as it was marked with <foreign xml:lang="gez">ዘአርብ፡</foreign> (= ‘Friday’) on <locus target="#56r"/> and 
                                    <foreign xml:lang="gez">ዘቀዳም፡</foreign> (= ‘Saturday’) on <locus target="#57v"/>.</note>
                                <incipit xml:lang="gez"><gap reason="lost"/>ምዓኒ፡ <add place="below">ቃ</add>ለ፡ ስዕለትየ፡ ከመ፡ ወልታ፡ ሥሙር፡ ከለልከነ፡
                                    <gap reason="omitted"/> ወበመቅሠፍትከ፡ ኢትገሥጸኒ፡ አንተ፡ እግዚኦ፡ ዕቀበነ፡ ወተማኅጸነነ፡ እምዛቲ፡ ትውልድ፡ ዘለዓን፡ ወበጽላሎተ፡ ክንፊከ፡
                                </incipit>
                                <explicit xml:lang="gez"><gap reason="lost"/> ቃልየ፡ ኀበ፡ እግዚአብሔር፡ ጸራኅኩ፡ ቃልየ፡ ኀበ፡ እግዚአብሔር፡ ሰአልኩ፡ ነጽር፡ ወትረ፡ ቃለ፡
                                    ስእለትየ፡ እስመ፡ ሐመምኩ፡ ፈድፋደ፡ ዘይሰማዕ፡ ግበር፡ ሊተ፡ ምሕረተከ፡ በጽባሕ፡ ወመንፈስከ፡ ቅዱስ፡ ይምርሐኒ፡ በምድረ፡ ጽድቅ፡ ይምርሐኒ፡ በምድረ፡ ጽድቅ፡
                                    ይትባረክ፡ እግዚአብሔር፡ አምላኪየ፡ መሐርየ፡ ወፀወንየ፡ ምስካይየ፡ ወመድኃንየ፡ ምዕመንየ፡</explicit>
                                <textLang xml:lang="gez"/>
                            </msItem> 
                            <msItem xml:id="p2_i2">
                                <locus from="61r" to="69r"/>
                                <title ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT1970Mashaf">Maṣḥafa taklil</title>
                                <note>Amharic interpretation of the ritual for the blessing of the spouses</note>
                                <incipit xml:lang="gez" type="inscriptio">መጽሐፈ፡ ተክሊል።</incipit>
                                <incipit xml:lang="am"><gap reason="omitted"/> ቆሞስ፡ ወይ፡ በርሱ፡ ፈቃድ፡ ያለ፡ ቄስ፡ በርሱ፡ ሰበካ፡ ያሉ፡ ሰዎች፡ የግቢ፡ ሥራት፡ 
                                    ሊያደርግላቸው፡ በጠሩት፡ ጊዜ፡ ካዋቆች፡ ሰዎች፡ የሚያደርጉ፡ ማንና፡ ማን፡ ናቸው፡ ብሎ፡ ይጠይቅ። ግቢ፡ የሚከለክል፡ ሕጋዊ፡ ምክንያት፡ ቢኖር፡ ባይኖር፡
                                    መርምሮ፡ እንዲያው። ዳግመኛም፡ በመዋደድ፡ እንዲሆን፡</incipit>
                                <textLang xml:lang="am" otherLangs="gez"/>
                            </msItem>
                            <msItem xml:id="p2_i3">
                                <locus from="69r" to="76r"/>
                                <title ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT1958Mashaf">Maṣḥafa qandil</title>
                                <incipit xml:lang="gez">በስመ፡ <gap reason="ellipsis"/> ንቀድም፡ በረድኤተ፡ እግዚአብ<surplus>፡</surplus>ሔር፡ ጽሒፈ፡ 
                                    መጽሐፈ፡ ቀንዲል። ይ፡ ካ፡ ረዳኢነ፡ ስመ፡ እግዚአብሔር። ይ፡ ሕ፡ ዘፈጠረ፡ ሰማየ፡ ወምድረ። ይ፡ ካ፡ እግዚአብሔር፡ ምስሌክሙ። ይ፡ ሕ፡ ወምስለ፡ ምንፈስከ።
                                    ይ፡ ካ፡ ንጸሊ፡ ኦእግዚኦ፡ ኢየሲስ፡ ክርስቶስ፡ ይባዕ፡ ውስተ፡ ዛቲ፡ ቤተ፡</incipit>
                                <textLang xml:lang="gez"/>
                            </msItem>
                            <msItem xml:id="p2_i4">
                                <locus from="76r" to="98r"/>
                                <title>Catholic prayers for the deceased</title>
                                <note>Containing explanations in Amharic interspersed into the text, for example on <locus target="#83v"/>:
                                    <foreign xml:lang="am">እግዚእነ፡ ኢየሱስ፡ ክርስቶስ፡ ዘህልው፡ ምስለ፡ አብ፡ ወመንፈስ፡ ቅዱስ፡ ወዘይነግሥ፡ 
                                        ለዓ<add place="below">ለ</add>መ፡ ዓለም። አሜን። ቢችል፡ ባለቤቱ፡ ባይችልም፡ ሌላ፡ የሚያደርግለት፡ ጸሎት፡ ይህ፡ ነው። ይ፡ ካ፡ ንሰግድ፡
                                        ለከ፡ ክርስቶስ፡</foreign>. 
                                    <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS2654Benedict"><roleName type="title">Pope</roleName> Benedict XV (1914-1922)</persName>
                                    is mentioned on <locus from="89v" to="90r"/>: <foreign xml:lang="gez">ሊቃነ፡ ጳጳሳት፡ <pb n="90r"/> እንተ፡ ሮማ፡ 
                                        በነዲክቶስ፡ ዘይሰመይ፡ ፒያማተር፡</foreign></note>
                                <incipit xml:lang="gez" type="inscriptio">ጸሎት፡ 
                                    ዘሙታ<choice resp="PRS8999Strelcyn"><sic>ል</sic><corr>ን</corr></choice>፡</incipit>
                                <incipit xml:lang="gez">ይ፡ ካ፡ ኪርየ፡ ኤለይሶን። ይ፡ ሕ፡ ክርስቴ፡ ኤለይሶን። ይ፡ ካ፡ ኪርየ፡ ኤለይሶን። ኦቅድስት፡ ማርያም። ሰአሊ፡ በእንቲአሁ። 
                                    <pb n="76v"/> ኦኵልክሙ፡ ቅዱሳት፡ መላእክት፡ ወሊቃነ፡ መላእ<add place="below">ክት።</add> ሰዓሉ፡ በእንቲአሁ። 
                                    <gap reason="omitted"/> ወቅዱስ፡ አቤል፡ ሰአል፡ በእንቲአሁ። ኦኵልክሙ፡ ጉባዔ፡ ጻድቃን። ሰአሉ፡ 
                                    <expan><abbr> በእ</abbr><ex>ንቲአሁ።</ex></expan> ኦቅዱስ፡ አብርሃም። ሰአል፡ በእንቲአሁ፡ ኦቅዱስ፡ ዮሐንስ፡ መጥምቅ። 
                                    ሰአል፡ <expan><abbr> በእ</abbr><ex>ንቲአሁ።</ex></expan> ኦቅዱስ፡ ዮሴፍ።</incipit>
                                <textLang xml:lang="gez" otherLangs="am"/>
                            </msItem>
                            <msItem xml:id="p2_i5">
                                <locus from="98r" to="104v"/>
                                <title type="incomplete">Catholic Litanies to the Saints Liṭānyā la-qǝddusāt</title>   
                                <note>The end is missing. Among the invoked saints, there are a large number of saints of the Catholic Church, e.g.:
                                    St Lawrence (<foreign xml:lang="gez">ለውረንሲዮስ፡</foreign>), St Sylvester (<foreign xml:lang="gez">ሲልበስተር፡</foreign>), 
                                    <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS1839Ambrose">St Ambrose</persName> (<foreign xml:lang="gez">አምብሮዝዮስ፡</foreign>),
                                    St Benedict (<foreign xml:lang="gez">በነዲክቶስ፡</foreign>), St Francis (<foreign xml:lang="gez">ፈረንሲስኩስ፡</foreign>), 
                                    St Lucy (<foreign xml:lang="gez">ሉስያ፡</foreign>).</note>
                                <incipit xml:lang="gez">ሊጣንያ፡ ለቅዱሳት። ይካ። ኪርኤ፡ ለይሶን። ይሕ፡ 
                                    ክ<supplied reason="omitted" resp="PRS8999Strelcyn">ር</supplied>ስቴ፡ ለይሶን። <pb n="98v"/> ይካ፡ ኪርየ፡ ኤለይሶን።
                                    ይካ፡ ኦክርስቶስ፡ አፅምአነ። ይሕ፡ ኦክርስቶስ፡ አፅምአነ።</incipit>
                                <textLang xml:lang="gez"/>
